            <div xml:id="d773">

                <pb facs="0731" n="719" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg719"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.857 Hannover/14: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Venezuela</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Corrigan</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-04-11T14:00:00-04:30">April 11, 1940—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 5:33 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>36. Department’s circular April 6, 3 p.m. The Mexican [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Venezuelan?</hi>] Minister for Foreign Affairs reaffirmed the position of
                    his Government that the correct method of procedure is by submission of all
                    protests to the Rio Neutrality Committee (please see last paragraph of
                    memorandum transmitted with my despatch 230, February 21, 1940<anchor n="41"
                        xml:id="d773-f1"/>). He has communicated with Dr. Garay to this effect.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Corrigan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
